./" Manpage for cpvi 
.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	cpvi - cp a file then edit it in vim (the copy not the original)
.SH SYNOPSIS
	cpvi source destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	does cp then edits the copied file in vim
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose. Copies directories by default (-r) \n\n
	vim default options do not work
.SH EXAMPLES
	cpvi hi.csv csvs
	cpvi sdifji.py ../../ijsdif/jsissbsbbsb.py
	cpvi 1.txt 2.txt
.SH BUGS
	probably none
